I step off the water metro at Fort Kochi.
It is very hot outside.
There is a small spice shop nearby here.
I need to get to that shop.
I walk directly to the shop.
I step inside the shop.
A person is standing there.
I smile at him.
"Namaskaram, what do you need?" he asks.
"Namaskaram," I say.
"I need a packet of black pepper."
"This is for my family."
"They are in Mexico."
"Do you have fresh black pepper?"
He nods happily.
He gives me a packet.
"This is fresh, it is very good black pepper," he says.
I pay the money.
My family will certainly like the black pepper from Kochi.
